  "answer": "To reduce the risk of unconstrained reinforcement-learning policies causing damage or violating safety constraints, fine-tuning agents with Constrained Policy Optimization (CPO) has been proposed (https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.10528). This approach ensures that intermediate neural network policies respect safety limits through trust region optimization under Constrained Markov Decision Process (CMDP) constraints (https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.10528). The mechanism relies on performance bounds that link KL-divergence to changes in expected return and constraints, providing an update rule that limits constraint violations and bounds potential reward decreases (https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.10528). Specifically, CPO linearises the objectives and forms quadratic surrogate constraints, solves a small dual problem for variables λ and ν, and employs backtracking via a line search to satisfy these surrogate constraints, thereby guaranteeing per-update constraint satisfaction (https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.10528)."
